    "body": "@zcorpan Generally LGTM. Only one nitpick - I've noticed that spec uses only \"set the temporary buffer to the empty string\" and \"append ... character to the temporary buffer\" operations on temporary buffer (as if string and a character are incompatible types, which they are in some languages), so tried to avoid introduction of new operation for direct \"set the temporary buffer to ... character\".\n\nPerhaps better to maintain this property for consistency and just add \"set the temporary buffer to the empty string\" before the \"append\"?\n",
